  "runtime_requirements": [
    "Shim verifies its actual kernel extent and entry x0 against input windows before writing the FD destination.",
    "SEC copies the bounded FDT before initializing the heap/MMU and logs CurrentEL, SCTLR, CNTFRQ, kernel/x0/initrd addresses.",
    "initrd is validated in 64-bit arithmetic against protected/control regions and copied with overlap-safe semantics to payload_copy; no input corridor becomes pool memory.",
    "Only dxe_heap is published as allocator RAM. Boot memory driver must not import the remaining 12 GB.",
    "Framebuffer uses only a verified subrange of the splash reservation; no pool allocations use display memory.",
    "The old header addresses 0x8000/0x1000000/0x1f00000 are ABL input fields. They are not physical RAM mappings.",
    "Static pass cannot prove secure firmware carveouts absent from FDT, ABL placement or memory surviving reset; unexpected runtime ranges fail closed."
  ]
